+<HR>
+<DL>
+<DT><PRE><FONT SIZE="-1"><A HREF="http://hc.apache.org/httpcomponents-core-ga/httpcore/apidocs/org/apache/http/annotation/NotThreadSafe.html" title="class or interface in org.apache.http.annotation">@NotThreadSafe</A>
+</FONT>public class <B>BasicManagedEntity</B><DT>extends <A HREF="http://hc.apache.org/httpcomponents-core-ga/httpcore/apidocs/org/apache/http/entity/HttpEntityWrapper.html" title="class or interface in org.apache.http.entity">HttpEntityWrapper</A><DT>implements <A HREF="../../../../org/apache/http/conn/ConnectionReleaseTrigger.html" title="interface in org.apache.http.conn">ConnectionReleaseTrigger</A>, <A HREF="../../../../org/apache/http/conn/EofSensorWatcher.html" title="interface in org.apache.http.conn">EofSensorWatcher</A></DL>
+</PRE>
+
+<P>
+An entity that releases a <A HREF="../../../../org/apache/http/conn/ManagedClientConnection.html" title="interface in org.apache.http.conn"><CODE>connection</CODE></A>.
+ A <A HREF="../../../../org/apache/http/conn/ManagedClientConnection.html" title="interface in org.apache.http.conn"><CODE>ManagedClientConnection</CODE></A> will
+ typically <i>not</i> return a managed entity, but you can replace
+ the unmanaged entity in the response with a managed one.
+<P>
