+
+<A NAME="getKeepAliveDuration(org.apache.http.HttpResponse, org.apache.http.protocol.HttpContext)"><!-- --></A><H3>
+getKeepAliveDuration</H3>
+<PRE>
+long <B>getKeepAliveDuration</B>(<A HREF="http://hc.apache.org/httpcomponents-core-ga/httpcore/apidocs/org/apache/http/HttpResponse.html" title="class or interface in org.apache.http">HttpResponse</A>&nbsp;response,
+                          <A HREF="http://hc.apache.org/httpcomponents-core-ga/httpcore/apidocs/org/apache/http/protocol/HttpContext.html" title="class or interface in org.apache.http.protocol">HttpContext</A>&nbsp;context)</PRE>
+<DL>
+<DD>Returns the duration of time which this connection can be safely kept
+ idle. If the connection is left idle for longer than this period of time,
+ it MUST not reused. A value of 0 or less may be returned to indicate that
+ there is no suitable suggestion.
+
+ When coupled with a <A HREF="http://hc.apache.org/httpcomponents-core-ga/httpcore/apidocs/org/apache/http/ConnectionReuseStrategy.html" title="class or interface in org.apache.http"><CODE>ConnectionReuseStrategy</CODE></A>, if
+ <A HREF="http://hc.apache.org/httpcomponents-core-ga/httpcore/apidocs/org/apache/http/ConnectionReuseStrategy.html#keepAlive(org.apache.http.HttpResponse, org.apache.http.protocol.HttpContext)" title="class or interface in org.apache.http"><CODE>ConnectionReuseStrategy.keepAlive(HttpResponse, HttpContext)</CODE></A>
+ returns true, this allows you to control how long the reuse will last. If
+ keepAlive returns false, this should have no meaningful impact
+<P>
+<DD><DL>
+<DT><B>Parameters:</B><DD><CODE>response</CODE> - The last response received over the connection.<DD><CODE>context</CODE> - the context in which the connection is being used.
+<DT><B>Returns:</B><DD>the duration in ms for which it is safe to keep the connection
+         idle, or <=0 if no suggested duration.</DL>
+</DD>
+</DL>
+<!-- ========= END OF CLASS DATA ========= -->
