+<A NAME="shouldBackoff(java.lang.Throwable)"><!-- --></A><H3>
+shouldBackoff</H3>
+<PRE>
+public boolean <B>shouldBackoff</B>(<A HREF="http://download.oracle.com/javase/1.5.0/docs/api/java/lang/Throwable.html" title="class or interface in java.lang">Throwable</A>&nbsp;t)</PRE>
+<DL>
+<DD><B>Description copied from interface: <CODE><A HREF="../../../../../org/apache/http/client/ConnectionBackoffStrategy.html#shouldBackoff(java.lang.Throwable)">ConnectionBackoffStrategy</A></CODE></B></DD>
+<DD>Determines whether seeing the given <code>Throwable</code> as
+ a result of request execution should result in a backoff
+ signal.
+<P>
+<DD><DL>
+<DT><B>Specified by:</B><DD><CODE><A HREF="../../../../../org/apache/http/client/ConnectionBackoffStrategy.html#shouldBackoff(java.lang.Throwable)">shouldBackoff</A></CODE> in interface <CODE><A HREF="../../../../../org/apache/http/client/ConnectionBackoffStrategy.html" title="interface in org.apache.http.client">ConnectionBackoffStrategy</A></CODE></DL>
+</DD>
+<DD><DL>
+<DT><B>Parameters:</B><DD><CODE>t</CODE> - the <code>Throwable</code> that happened
+<DT><B>Returns:</B><DD><code>true</code> if a backoff signal should be
+   given</DL>
+</DD>
+</DL>
+<HR>
+
+<A NAME="shouldBackoff(org.apache.http.HttpResponse)"><!-- --></A><H3>
+shouldBackoff</H3>
+<PRE>
+public boolean <B>shouldBackoff</B>(<A HREF="http://hc.apache.org/httpcomponents-core-ga/httpcore/apidocs/org/apache/http/HttpResponse.html" title="class or interface in org.apache.http">HttpResponse</A>&nbsp;resp)</PRE>
+<DL>
+<DD><B>Description copied from interface: <CODE><A HREF="../../../../../org/apache/http/client/ConnectionBackoffStrategy.html#shouldBackoff(org.apache.http.HttpResponse)">ConnectionBackoffStrategy</A></CODE></B></DD>
+<DD>Determines whether receiving the given <A HREF="http://hc.apache.org/httpcomponents-core-ga/httpcore/apidocs/org/apache/http/HttpResponse.html" title="class or interface in org.apache.http"><CODE>HttpResponse</CODE></A> as
+ a result of request execution should result in a backoff
+ signal. Implementations MUST restrict themselves to examining
+ the response header and MUST NOT consume any of the response
+ body, if any.
+<P>
+<DD><DL>
+<DT><B>Specified by:</B><DD><CODE><A HREF="../../../../../org/apache/http/client/ConnectionBackoffStrategy.html#shouldBackoff(org.apache.http.HttpResponse)">shouldBackoff</A></CODE> in interface <CODE><A HREF="../../../../../org/apache/http/client/ConnectionBackoffStrategy.html" title="interface in org.apache.http.client">ConnectionBackoffStrategy</A></CODE></DL>
+</DD>
+<DD><DL>
+<DT><B>Parameters:</B><DD><CODE>resp</CODE> - the <code>HttpResponse</code> that was received
+<DT><B>Returns:</B><DD><code>true</code> if a backoff signal should be
+   given</DL>
+</DD>
+</DL>
