+</DL>
+<HR>
+
+<A NAME="set(byte[])"><!-- --></A><H3>
+set</H3>
+<PRE>
+void <B>set</B>(byte[]&nbsp;bytes)</PRE>
+<DL>
+<DD>Given a serialized representation of a <A HREF="../../../../../../../org/apache/http/impl/client/cache/memcached/MemcachedCacheEntry.html" title="interface in org.apache.http.impl.client.cache.memcached"><CODE>MemcachedCacheEntry</CODE></A>,
+ attempt to reconstitute the storage key and <A HREF="../../../../../../../org/apache/http/client/cache/HttpCacheEntry.html" title="class in org.apache.http.client.cache"><CODE>HttpCacheEntry</CODE></A>
+ represented therein. After a successful call to this method, this
+ object should return updated (as appropriate) values for
+ <A HREF="../../../../../../../org/apache/http/impl/client/cache/memcached/MemcachedCacheEntry.html#getStorageKey()"><CODE>getStorageKey()</CODE></A> and <A HREF="../../../../../../../org/apache/http/impl/client/cache/memcached/MemcachedCacheEntry.html#getHttpCacheEntry()"><CODE>getHttpCacheEntry()</CODE></A>. This
+ should be viewed as an atomic operation on the
+ <code>MemcachedCacheEntry</code>.
+<P>
+<DD><DL>
+<DT><B>Parameters:</B><DD><CODE>bytes</CODE> - serialized representation
+<DT><B>Throws:</B>
+<DD><CODE>{@link</CODE> - MemcachedSerializationException} if deserialization
+   fails. In this case, the prior values for {<A HREF="../../../../../../../org/apache/http/impl/client/cache/memcached/MemcachedCacheEntry.html#getStorageKey()"><CODE>getStorageKey()</CODE></A>
+   and <A HREF="../../../../../../../org/apache/http/impl/client/cache/memcached/MemcachedCacheEntry.html#getHttpCacheEntry()"><CODE>getHttpCacheEntry()</CODE></A> should remain unchanged.</DL>
+</DD>
+</DL>
